<misterromdescription>
    <name>Tank Cocktail</name>
    <setname>tankc</setname>
    <parent>tank</parent>
    <rbf>Tank</rbf>
    <mameversion>0289</mameversion>
    <about>Tank cocktail table (Kee Games / Atari, 1974, TM-036). Same Panzer
Board #1/#2 (A003110/A003112) and ROM as the upright (MAME: tank, "Tank/Tank
Cocktail"); the face-up XM501 monitor is turned 90 degrees between the two
players, and harness 004032 drives one speaker per tank (WH TANK / BK TANK).
Rotation is HDMI-only; switch Monitor to CCW if your mounting is the other way.</about>
    <year>1974</year>
    <manufacturer>Kee Games (Atari)</manufacturer>
    <category>Shooter / Maze</category>
    <players>2 (simultaneous, cocktail)</players>
    <joystick>2 x 2-way (twin sticks per player)</joystick>
    <rotation>Vertical (CW)</rotation>

    <rom index="0" zip="tank.zip" md5="a18a083787ddf84ac6e8a0d1be67b906">
        <part name="90-2006.k10" crc="87f5c365"/>
    </rom>

    <!-- Byte 0 [1:0] = monitor orientation: default Cocktail CW -->
    <switches default="01">
        <dip bits="0,1" name="Monitor" ids="Upright,Cocktail CW,Cocktail CCW"/>
    </switches>
</misterromdescription>
